From: Felipe Correa da Silva Sanches <juca@members.fsf.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:59:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] ttf: a font without glyph classes gets none

Without GDEF glyph classes a shaper guesses each glyph's class as it is used: from
its codepoint, or kept through a substitution, so the same glyph can be a mark
after a substitution of U+0301 and a base when its own (private-use) codepoint is
typed. No class table can say that, and a compiler writes one as soon as a glyph
is a mark. Every glyph of such a font is now a base, so the compiled font has no
glyph classes either and shapes as the binary does (PT Serif: 13995 of 2250538
runs differed, as accents ccmp substitutes kept their advance; none now). A legacy
kern pair is still left out when the shaper would take a glyph of it for a mark.

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
